Input: {"question": "Who led the Chola invasion of Kalinga?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0165-03603b88adca:d00", "start": 0, "end": 169, "text": "Chola invasion of Kalinga (1097) The first Chola invasion of Kalinga by Kulothunga Chola I in 1097 was intended to avenge the invasion of Vengi by the forces of Kalinga."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0165-03603b88adca:d00", "start": 170, "end": 292, "text": "The war resulted in the subjugation of Kalinga and its reduction to the position of a tributary state of the Chola Empire."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0165-03603b88adca:d00", "start": 293, "end": 403, "text": "In 1097, the army of Kalinga invaded the Eastern Chalukya kingdom which was then a vassal of the Chola Empire."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0165-03603b88adca:d00", "start": 404, "end": 476, "text": "The troops of Kalinga were supported by the chief of Kolanu near Ellore."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0165-03603b88adca:d00", "start": 477, "end": 542, "text": "A huge army under Vikrama Chola was sent to repulse the invaders."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0165-03603b88adca:d00", "start": 543, "end": 555, "text": "The army was"}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0165-03603b88adca:d01", "start": 0, "end": 279, "text": "Chola invasion of Kalinga '' 1097 – news · newspapers · books · scholar · JSTOR ( August 2019 ) ( Learn how and when to remove this message ) The first Chola invasion of Kalinga by Kulothunga Chola I in 1097 was intended to avenge the invasion of Vengi by the forces of Kalinga ."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0165-03603b88adca:d01", "start": 280, "end": 409, "text": "[ 1 ] The war resulted in the subjugation of Kalinga and its reduction to the position of a tributary state of the Chola Empire ."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0165-03603b88adca:d01", "start": 410, "end": 460, "text": "Chola invasion of Kalinga ( 1097 ) Date 1097 C.E ."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0165-03603b88adca:d01", "start": 461, "end": 518, "text": "Location Kalinga Result Chola victory Territorial changes"}, "D3S1": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0165-03603b88adca:d02", "start": 0, "end": 207, "text": "Chola invasion of Kalinga (1110) The Chola invasion of Kalinga in 1110 CE was the second and more famous of the two campaigns against the kingdom of Kalinga undertaken during the reign of Kulothunga Chola I."}, "D3S2": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0165-03603b88adca:d02", "start": 208, "end": 367, "text": "The forces led by the Pallava chief, Karunakara Tondaiman, achieved an easy victory over the army of Kalinga forcing its king, Anantavarman Chodaganga to flee."}, "D3S3": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0165-03603b88adca:d02", "start": 368, "end": 442, "text": "The war and its causes form the subject of the ballad, \"Kalingattuparani\"."}, "D3S4": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0165-03603b88adca:d02", "start": 443, "end": 585, "text": "The kingdom of Kalinga had been subdued in the first Chola invasion of Kalinga and the king had become a vassal of the Cholas paying an annual"}, "D4S1": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0165-03603b88adca:d03", "start": 0, "end": 652, "text": "dbc :1110_in_Asia dbc : Conflicts_in_1110 dbc : Military_campaigns_involving_the_Chola_Empire rdf : type yago : WikicatConflictsIn1110 yago : WikicatMilitaryCampaignsInvolvingTheCholaEmpire yago : Abstraction100002137 yago : Act100030358 yago : Activity100407535 yago : Campaign100968155 yago : Conflict100958896 yago : Event100029378 yago : GroupAction101080366 yago : Operation100955060 yago : PsychologicalFeature100023100 yago : YagoPermanentlyLocatedEntity rdfs : comment The Chola invasion of Kalinga in 1110 CE was the second and more famous of the two campaigns against